  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1953\n£10.00\n\n7 available\nThe Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1953 quantity\nAdd to Cart\n\nCompiled and Edited by Brigadier-General C. G. Higgins, C.M.G., D.S.O., D.L. Volume LV January to December 1953.\n\nPublished 1954 - Slatter & Rose Oxford. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List -p.1\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette' 1953 -p.3\n\nRegular Officers of the Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed on December 31st, 1952 -p.14\n\nRecords of the First Battalion -p.35\n\nSummary of the First Battalion Diary 1953 -p.19\n\nFirst Battalion Letter -p.35\n\nFirst Battalion Records of Sport and Training -p.40\n\nRecords of Regimental Headquarters -p.62\n\nRegimental Headquarters Letter -p.63\n\nRecords of the Fourth Battalion -p.68\n\nFourth Battalion Letter -p.71\n\nRegimental Dinner 1953 -p.76\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner -p.77\n\n52nd Light Infantry Luncheon -p.78\n\nMarch of the First Battalion Through Oxford -p.80\n\nPresentation by the Hauraki Regiment-p.84\n\nBrief History of the Hauraki Regiment -p.88\n\nLight Infantry Brigade -p.93\n\nThe Commonwealth Division in Korea 1952-53 -p.105\n\nThe Coronation: Inside the abbey and Out -p.115\n\nTwelve Months' Malingering -p.130\n\nGun Days -p.136\n\nImpressions of the Free territory of Trieste -p.146\n\nMargate Platform, May 1940 -p.150\n\nAn Army Marches On It's Stomach -p.159\n\nNow and Then -p.167\n\nHorses at Osnabruck -p.171\n\nLeave in Lebanon -p.176.\n\nOfficers' Mess Silver and Pictures - First Battalion -p.181\n\nThe Indian Mutiny Medal Rolls -p.190\n\nDress Regulations - Officers -p.193\n\nRegimental Cricket Week -p.197\n\nOld Comrades' Association -p.201\n\nHistorical Record of the 43rd Light Infantry (completed) -p.204\n\nObituary -p.239\n\nIndex -p.263\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nRedcoats to Riflemen: A Short History of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire County Regiment\n£4.50 Add to cart\nWinston Churchill: Oxfordshire Hussar – A Bugle & Sabre Special\n£2.00 Add to cart\nThe Skipper’s War: Dragon School, Oxford & The Great War\n£20.00 Add to cart\nIdentifying Cap Badges: A Family Historian’s Guide\n£25.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
